      /    \
C(10)  (12)
     0     /  \
       A(5) B(7)
          0    1
Character  Huffman Code: A 10, B 11, C 0.

Q3. Why Huffman coding is lossless compression?
Huffman coding is called lossless compression because the original data can be recovered exactly without losing any information.
Reasons:
Every character has a unique binary code.
It uses prefix-free codes, meaning no code is the prefix of another code.
The encoded data can be decoded using the Huffman Tree.
No original information is lost during compression.

